From 9438d431a07f03bfb2a78fd3d42573ade4591a6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hoangvu12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:02:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Docker sign-in: a gone host device is none, and the dialog
 hears a failed sign-in
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the Laptop (2026-11-17) "Sign in with Docker" waited forever after Vu
approved the code. The registry still named Docker's host device as one
the account no longer had (written while testing the day before), so the
key went there once the sign-in finished, wasn't taken, and was forgotten
on the Laptop. That was only logged (tracing::warn!), and the dialog kept
asking that device for the account. Docker's own device flow was fine:
run for real against login.docker.com, the poll took the approval.

- settle_host: a named host device that isn't among the account's devices
  is none, so the device that connected picks again (only once the device
  list has loaded, so a real host is never passed over).
- The background sign-in's end is kept with the provider and listed by
  ListSandboxProviders as `connect {userCode, error?}`: Docker refusing
  it, its code running out, or the key not reaching the host device.
- Settings › Sandboxes asks this device's engine for it while the code
  shows: a failure or an expired code (its own timeout too) replaces the
  wait with the reason and Try again, which asks for a new code.
